    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://arxiv.org/abs/2104.08812">
        <z:itemType>conferencePaper</z:itemType>
        <dcterms:isPartOf>
            <bib:Journal>
                <dc:title>Proceedings of the 2021 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing</dc:title>
                <dc:identifier>DOI 10.18653/v1/2021.emnlp-main.84</dc:identifier>
            </bib:Journal>
        </dcterms:isPartOf>
        <bib:authors>
            <rdf:Seq>
                <rdf:li>
                    <foaf:Person>
                        <foaf:surname>Zhou</foaf:surname>
                        <foaf:givenName>Wenxuan</foaf:givenName>
                    </foaf:Person>
                </rdf:li>
                <rdf:li>
                    <foaf:Person>
                        <foaf:surname>Liu</foaf:surname>
                        <foaf:givenName>Fangyu</foaf:givenName>
                    </foaf:Person>
                </rdf:li>
                <rdf:li>
                    <foaf:Person>
                        <foaf:surname>Chen</foaf:surname>
                        <foaf:givenName>Muhao</foaf:givenName>
                    </foaf:Person>
                </rdf:li>
            </rdf:Seq>
        </bib:authors>
        <dcterms:isReferencedBy rdf:resource="#item_89"/>
        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_91"/>
        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_90"/>
        <dc:relation rdf:resource="http://arxiv.org/abs/2308.10261"/>
        <dc:relation rdf:resource="#item_80"/>
        <dc:subject>
            <z:AutomaticTag>
               <rdf:value>Computer Science - Computation and Language</rdf:value>
            </z:AutomaticTag>
        </dc:subject>
        <dc:title>Contrastive Out-of-Distribution Detection for Pretrained Transformers</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>Pretrained Transformers achieve remarkable performance when training and test data are from the same distribution. However, in real-world scenarios, the model often faces out-of-distribution (OOD) instances that can cause severe semantic shift problems at inference time. Therefore, in practice, a reliable model should identify such instances, and then either reject them during inference or pass them over to models that handle another distribution. In this paper, we develop an unsupervised OOD detection method, in which only the in-distribution (ID) data are used in training. We propose to fine-tune the Transformers with a contrastive loss, which improves the compactness of representations, such that OOD instances can be better differentiated from ID ones. These OOD instances can then be accurately detected using the Mahalanobis distance in the model's penultimate layer. We experiment with comprehensive settings and achieve near-perfect OOD detection performance, outperforming baselines drastically. We further investigate the rationales behind the improvement, finding that more compact representations through margin-based contrastive learning bring the improvement. We release our code to the community for future research.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>2021</dc:date>
        <z:libraryCatalog>arXiv.org</z:libraryCatalog>
        <dc:identifier>
            <dcterms:URI>
               <rdf:value>http://arxiv.org/abs/2104.08812</rdf:value>
            </dcterms:URI>
        </dc:identifier>
        <dcterms:dateSubmitted>2025-04-17 09:57:48</dcterms:dateSubmitted>
        <dc:description>arXiv:2104.08812 [cs]</dc:description>
        <bib:pages>1100-1111</bib:pages>
    </rdf:Description>
    <bib:Memo rdf:about="#item_89">
        <rdf:value>&lt;div data-schema-version=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Comment: Accepted at EMNLP 2021. Code available at https://github.com/wzhouad/Contra-OOD&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(255, 212, 0, 0.5)&quot;&gt;My comments: intéressant, prouve encore que représentation base methods fonctionne mieux, teste que décoder only models (BERT, ROBERTa) et méthode qui requiert fine-tuning complet sur les ID data only mais il faut ajuster les paramètres du fine-tuning et en plus LoRA ou d’autres méthodes plus frugales n’ont pas été testées.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pretrained transformers (like BERT, RoBERTa) perform well on in-distribution (ID) data but &lt;strong&gt;fail to detect out-of-distribution (OOD)&lt;/strong&gt; inputs reliably, especially under &lt;strong&gt;semantic shift&lt;/strong&gt; — when inputs come from &lt;strong&gt;unknown classes or tasks&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key gap:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Most prior NLP OOD detection methods:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Assume OOD data is available during training (often not the case in real applications).
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Use only confidence-based heuristics (e.g., max softmax probability), which can misclassify OOD inputs with high confidence.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Proposed Method: Contrastive Learning for OOD Detection&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The authors introduce an &lt;strong&gt;unsupervised OOD detection framework&lt;/strong&gt; using only &lt;strong&gt;ID data&lt;/strong&gt; and propose a &lt;strong&gt;contrastive learning approach&lt;/strong&gt; to improve the &lt;strong&gt;representational space&lt;/strong&gt; of pretrained transformers:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contrastive Learning&lt;/strong&gt; encourages:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Similar class instances to form &lt;strong&gt;compact clusters&lt;/strong&gt;.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Different classes to be &lt;strong&gt;pushed apart&lt;/strong&gt; in embedding space.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two types of contrastive loss are studied:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Supervised contrastive loss&lt;/strong&gt; (grouping same-class instances).
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Margin-based contrastive loss&lt;/strong&gt; (encourages minimum distance margin between different classes).
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Mahalanobis distance&lt;/strong&gt; is used as the OOD detection score, computed from the &lt;strong&gt;penultimate layer&lt;/strong&gt; of the model.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Evaluate on 4 models (&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 32, 32)&quot;&gt;decoder &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;only):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;BERT-Base&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;BERT-Large&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;RoBERTa-Base&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;RoBERTa-Large&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Datasets: &lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #ff2020&quot;&gt;There is only &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #ff2020&quot;&gt;FAR-OOD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #ff2020&quot;&gt; datasets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; data-attachment-key=&quot;2VTRP3F3&quot; width=&quot;684&quot; height=&quot;365&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; data-attachment-key=&quot;76YCQK8G&quot; width=&quot;681&quot; height=&quot;342&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Results: How well does it perform?&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
The &lt;strong&gt;margin-based contrastive loss + &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 32, 32)&quot;&gt;Mahalanobis distance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; achieves &lt;strong&gt;state-of-the-art OOD detection&lt;/strong&gt; on 4 NLP classification tasks (SST2, IMDB, TREC-10, 20 Newsgroups).
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Outperforms baseline methods using:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Max softmax probability (MSP),
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Energy-based scores,
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Cosine similarity.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Shows &lt;strong&gt;near-perfect OOD detection&lt;/strong&gt; in some cases (AUROC &amp;gt; 99%, FAR95 &amp;lt; 2%).
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;u&gt;Important findings:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Contrastive learning improves OOD separation without harming in-distribution classification accuracy.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Larger models and richer pretraining (e.g., RoBERTa vs. BERT) improve OOD performance.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Limitations:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
The performance boost is smaller in &lt;strong&gt;novel class detection&lt;/strong&gt;, where OOD inputs come from the same task domain.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Contrastive learning adds training complexity&lt;/strong&gt; and may require careful hyperparameter tuning.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
They &lt;strong&gt;fully fine-tune&lt;/strong&gt; the entire Transformer model &lt;strong&gt;on ID data only&lt;/strong&gt; to implement their solution (we don’t know for instance if LoRA would work or not)
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
The method only improves OOD detection, not general downstream performance.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;==&amp;gt; &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 32, 32)&quot;&gt;Mahalanobis distance &amp;gt; cosine similarity &amp;gt;&amp;gt; Energy, MSP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 32, 32)&quot;&gt;=&amp;gt; Therefore Representation based methods &amp;gt; Logtis based methods&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contrastive Out-of-Distribution Detection for Pretrained Transformers&lt;/strong&gt; – &lt;em&gt;Wenxuan Zhou, Fangyu Liu, Muhao Chen (EMNLP 2021).&lt;/em&gt; This work addresses OOD detection in NLP with no access to OOD samples during training (unsupervised OOD detection). It fine-tunes BERT/RoBERTa classifiers using a &lt;strong&gt;supervised contrastive loss (margin-based)&lt;/strong&gt; to produce &lt;strong&gt;compact in-distribution representations&lt;/strong&gt;, then applies a Mahalanobis distance detector​. The compact embeddings make unseen classes easier to distinguish. The method achieved &lt;strong&gt;near-perfect OOD detection&lt;/strong&gt; on several text classification tasks, &lt;strong&gt;dramatically outperforming&lt;/strong&gt; previous baselines​. &lt;em&gt;Models:&lt;/em&gt; BERT-base and RoBERTa (fine-tuned with contrastive learning). &lt;em&gt;Type:&lt;/em&gt; OOD detection (no OOD training data, uses ID training + contrastive objective). &lt;em&gt;NLP-specific:&lt;/em&gt; Yes, focused on text classification. &lt;em&gt;Benchmarks:&lt;/em&gt; Evaluated on multiple NLP datasets (e.g. SNIPS, CLINC, 20 Newsgroups, SST-2 sentiment, etc., combining in-domain vs. out-of-domain pairs as in prior works). &lt;em&gt;Key result:&lt;/em&gt; Contrastively fine-tuned transformers + Mahalanobis distance yielded &lt;strong&gt;drastically improved OOD accuracy&lt;/strong&gt;, often reaching near 100% AUROC in experiments​.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</rdf:value>
    </bib:Memo>
