        <dcterms:isReferencedBy rdf:resource="#item_267"/>
        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_266"/>
        <dc:title>Self-Alignment for Factuality: Mitigating Hallucinations in LLMs via Self-Evaluation</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>Despite showing impressive abilities, large language models (LLMs) often struggle with factual inaccuracies, i.e., ”hallucinations”, even when they hold relevant knowledge. To mitigate these hallucinations, current approaches typically necessitate high-quality human factuality annotations. In this work, we explore Self-Alignment for Factuality, where we leverage the self-evaluation capability of an LLM to provide training signals that steer the model towards factuality. Specifically, we incorporate Self-Eval, a self-evaluation component, to prompt an LLM to validate the factuality of its own generated responses solely based on its internal knowledge. Additionally, we design Self-Knowledge Tuning (SK-Tuning) to augment the LLM`s self-evaluation ability by improving the model`s confidence estimation and calibration. We then utilize these self-annotated responses to fine-tune the model via Direct Preference Optimization algorithm. We show that the proposed self-alignment approach substantially enhances factual accuracy over Llama family models across three key knowledge-intensive tasks on TruthfulQA and BioGEN.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>2024-08</dc:date>
        <z:shortTitle>Self-Alignment for Factuality</z:shortTitle>
        <z:libraryCatalog>ACLWeb</z:libraryCatalog>
        <dc:identifier>
            <dcterms:URI>
               <rdf:value>https://aclanthology.org/2024.acl-long.107/</rdf:value>
            </dcterms:URI>
        </dc:identifier>
        <dcterms:dateSubmitted>2025-04-29 09:20:58</dcterms:dateSubmitted>
        <bib:pages>1946–1965</bib:pages>
        <bib:presentedAt>
           <bib:Conference><dc:title>ACL 2024</dc:title></bib:Conference>
        </bib:presentedAt>
    </rdf:Description>
    <bib:Memo rdf:about="#item_267">
        <rdf:value>&lt;div data-schema-version=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(255, 212, 0, 0.5)&quot;&gt;My comments: =&amp;gt; not really relevant, prompts the LLM, don’t look at internal states of the LLM, focus on hallucinations where the LLM knows but tells differently so ot is not really for OOD since the LLM knows in the first place. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
(&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 119, 0)&quot;&gt;Self-alignment for factuality: Mitigating hallucinations in llms via self-evaluation 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(235, 82, 247)&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 119, 0)&quot;&gt;: &lt;/span&gt;calculates the probability 𝑝 (𝑇 𝑟𝑢𝑒) to assess the factuality of the response to a boolean question, relying exclusively on the model’s internal knowledge. &lt;u&gt;Strengths&lt;/u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt; Uses the model’s internal knowledge for factual assessment, no external data needed. &lt;u&gt;Weaknesses&lt;/u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt; Limited awareness of unknown facts; may misjudge confidence in inaccuracies.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Improvement of: &lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 119, 0)&quot;&gt;(Language models (mostly) know what they know 2021)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;Introduction:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our approach encourages an LLM to generate prediction confidence scores using the factuality of its own generated responses through &lt;strong&gt;self-asking&lt;/strong&gt;. Subsequently, these scores are utilized as reward signals to fine-tune the model using the Direct Preference Optimization (DPO) algorithm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;This work introduces&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;Self-Alignment for Factuality&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;, a framework that uses an LLM's&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;self-evaluation capability&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;to reduce hallucinations. Key components include:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;Self-Eval&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;: Prompts the LLM to validate its responses' factuality using its internal knowledge.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Given a prompt q and a LLM M, SELF-EVAL, built on M, is tasked with assessing the validity of M’s response a, leveraging exclusively its own internal knowledge. This process is quantified as the probability p(True|q, a), which is formulated as follows: p(True|q, a) = fM(q, a). We propose to utilize True/False Q&amp;amp;A prompt as follows, termed as SELF-EVAL-P(TRUE). This prompt facilitates the LLM’s self-evaluation of factuality based on its inherent knowledge:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(170, 170, 170, 0.5)&quot;&gt;Instruction: Please evaluate the truthfulness&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(170, 170, 170, 0.5)&quot;&gt;of the proposed answer based on the given&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(170, 170, 170, 0.5)&quot;&gt;question and internal knowledge.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(170, 170, 170, 0.5)&quot;&gt;&amp;lt;Few-shot Prompts&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(170, 170, 170, 0.5)&quot;&gt;Question: &amp;lt;Question&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(170, 170, 170, 0.5)&quot;&gt;Proposed Answer: &amp;lt;Answer&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(170, 170, 170, 0.5)&quot;&gt;Is the proposed answer:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(170, 170, 170, 0.5)&quot;&gt;A. True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(170, 170, 170, 0.5)&quot;&gt;B. False&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(170, 170, 170, 0.5)&quot;&gt;The proposed answer is:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;where we anticipate either “A” or “B” as an answer. The probability p(True) signifies the extent to which an LLM&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;deems a generated answer (claim) valid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;SK-Tuning (Self Knowledge Tuning)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;: Enhances self-evaluation by improving confidence calibration and estimation. &lt;/span&gt;We introduce SK-TUNING to enhance the LLM’s internal knowledge awareness, i.e., prediction confidence estimation and calibration through sufficient tuning across heterogeneous knowledge oriented tasks.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;Fine-Tuning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;: Self-annotated responses are used with&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;Direct Preference Optimization (DPO)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;to align the model toward factual accuracy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;Result&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;: Significant improvement in factual accuracy for Llama models on&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;TruthfulQA&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;BioGEN&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;across multiple knowledge-intensive tasks.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(255, 102, 102, 0.5)&quot;&gt;We focus on mitigating a type of hallucination, where the LLM &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(255, 102, 102, 0.5)&quot;&gt;knows&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(255, 102, 102, 0.5)&quot;&gt; the response but &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(255, 102, 102, 0.5)&quot;&gt;tells&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(255, 102, 102, 0.5)&quot;&gt; otherwise. For instance, an LLM might generate an inaccurate response during one inference time but can provide a correct response at another time&lt;/span&gt;. =&amp;gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 32, 32)&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 32, 32)&quot;&gt;Lila: so if the LLM don’t know (OOD this method won’t help)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 32, 32)&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Tasks/Datasets:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3 tasks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Multi-Choice Question-Answering (MCQA)
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
shortform open-ended generation
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
long-form openended generation,
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2 benchmark datasets:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
TruthfulQA
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
BioGEN
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; data-attachment-key=&quot;WML9C542&quot; width=&quot;764&quot; height=&quot;513&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; data-attachment-key=&quot;QJR37A7Q&quot; width=&quot;694&quot; height=&quot;335&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Results:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Surpasses:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 119, 0)&quot;&gt;Dola: Decoding by contrasting layers improves factuality in large language models 2023&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 119, 0)&quot;&gt;Contrastive decoding: Open-ended text generation as optimization 2022&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 119, 0)&quot;&gt;Fine-tuning language models for factuality 2023&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</rdf:value>
    </bib:Memo>
