        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_765"/>
        <dc:subject>
            <z:AutomaticTag>
               <rdf:value>Computer Science - Computation and Language</rdf:value>
            </z:AutomaticTag>
        </dc:subject>
        <dc:title>GPTScore: Evaluate as You Desire</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>Generative Artificial Intelligence (AI) has enabled the development of sophisticated models that are capable of producing high-caliber text, images, and other outputs through the utilization of large pre-trained models. Nevertheless, assessing the quality of the generation is an even more arduous task than the generation itself, and this issue has not been given adequate consideration recently. This paper proposes a novel evaluation framework, GPTScore, which utilizes the emergent abilities (e.g., zero-shot instruction) of generative pre-trained models to score generated texts. There are 19 pre-trained models explored in this paper, ranging in size from 80M (e.g., FLAN-T5-small) to 175B (e.g., GPT3). Experimental results on four text generation tasks, 22 evaluation aspects, and corresponding 37 datasets demonstrate that this approach can effectively allow us to achieve what one desires to evaluate for texts simply by natural language instructions. This nature helps us overcome several long-standing challenges in text evaluation--how to achieve customized, multi-faceted evaluation without the need for annotated samples. We make our code publicly available at https://github.com/jinlanfu/GPTScore.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>2023-02-13</dc:date>
        <z:shortTitle>GPTScore</z:shortTitle>
        <z:libraryCatalog>arXiv.org</z:libraryCatalog>
        <dc:identifier>
            <dcterms:URI>
               <rdf:value>http://arxiv.org/abs/2302.04166</rdf:value>
            </dcterms:URI>
        </dc:identifier>
        <dcterms:dateSubmitted>2025-05-06 12:08:18</dcterms:dateSubmitted>
        <dc:description>arXiv:2302.04166 [cs]</dc:description>
        <dc:identifier>DOI 10.48550/arXiv.2302.04166</dc:identifier>
        <prism:number>arXiv:2302.04166</prism:number>
    </rdf:Description>
    <bib:Memo rdf:about="#item_767">
        <rdf:value>&lt;div data-schema-version=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgba(255, 212, 0, 0.5)&quot;&gt;My comments: not very relevant. Uses GPT to evaluate NLP tasks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Introduction:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
The paper proposes a flexible, training-free framework for evaluating the quality of generated text using pre-trained generative language models (PLMs) like GPT-3 and FLAN-T5.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
Instead of using rigid metrics like ROUGE or BLEU, GPTScore uses &lt;strong&gt;natural language instructions&lt;/strong&gt; to guide large language models (LLMs) in &lt;strong&gt;evaluating specific qualities&lt;/strong&gt; of a generated output, such as fluency, factuality, or relevance — all without requiring additional fine-tuning or reference texts.
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Instead of training a separate evaluation model, GPTScore exploits the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;zero-shot and few-shot instruction-following capabilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;of these large models to produce evaluation scores directly.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GPTScore uses&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 32, 32)&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 32, 32)&quot;&gt;decoder-only&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; generative models as &lt;strong&gt;evaluators&lt;/strong&gt;, based on the principle that:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If a generated text aligns well with the task and a specified evaluation aspect (like &quot;Is it factual?&quot;), then the model should assign it a &lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;high conditional log-probability&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In contrast to prior approaches that apply a &lt;strong&gt;fixed confidence measure&lt;/strong&gt; (like raw log-probability), GPTScore refines this by &lt;strong&gt;conditioning the evaluation&lt;/strong&gt; on:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
A task-specific instruction,
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
An aspect definition (e.g., fluency),
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
The input context or source text, and optionally,
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
A few example prompts (in-context demonstrations).
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Method&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Input Preparation:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;For each evaluation instance, the method constructs a&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;prompt template&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;that includes:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;input context or source&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;(e.g., source text for summarization or translation).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;aspect to evaluate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;(e.g., &quot;Evaluate the factual correctness&quot;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;A&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;task description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;or instruction that guides the model on what to focus on.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Optionally,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;demonstrations/examples&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;of good evaluations to improve performance via in-context learning.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Feeding the Prompt:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;The generated text (candidate output) to be evaluated is appended to the prompt.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;This combined prompt is fed into the generative PLM.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Scoring Mechanism:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;The model computes the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 32, 32)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 32, 32)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;log-likelihoods&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 32, 32)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;of the tokens in the candidate text given the prompt.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;These token-level probabilities are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;weighted and aggregated&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;into a single scalar score called the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;GPTScore&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;The score reflects how well the candidate text aligns with the instructed evaluation aspect:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; data-attachment-key=&quot;VWH7UHP9&quot; width=&quot;459&quot; height=&quot;76&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: inherit&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Key Features&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Customizable and Multi-Aspect: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Users can specify&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;any&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;evaluation aspect via natural language instructions, enabling&amp;nbsp;customized and multi-faceted evaluation&amp;nbsp;without needing labeled datasets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Training-Free: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;GPTScore requires&amp;nbsp;no additional training or fine-tuning&amp;nbsp;of the evaluator model. It relies on the inherent zero-shot or few-shot abilities of the PLMs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Wide Model Support: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;The paper explores 19 different PLMs ranging from 80 million to 175 billion parameters, including FLAN-T5 and GPT-3 variants.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Broad Applicability: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;GPTScore is tested on&amp;nbsp;four text generation tasks&amp;nbsp;(e.g., summarization, translation) across&amp;nbsp;22 evaluation aspects&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;37 datasets, demonstrating strong performance and flexibility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: inherit&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Implementation Details&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Instruction and Demonstration Usage:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;The framework supports three modes:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Using both&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;instructions and demonstrations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;(best performance).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Using&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;instructions only&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Using&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;neither&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;(baseline).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Example Usage:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;To evaluate the quality of generated text on a dataset like BAGEL, users set flags to enable GPTScore with or without instructions and demonstrations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;The system outputs scores that reflect the desired evaluation aspect.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Open Source:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;The code is publicly available, allowing easy adoption and adaptation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: inherit&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Why GPTScore Matters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Overcomes Traditional Limitations:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Traditional evaluation metrics often rely on reference texts and fixed criteria.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;GPTScore’s instruction-driven approach allows&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;reference-free evaluation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;tailored criteria&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;without costly annotation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Leverages Emergent Model Abilities:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Large PLMs have shown surprising capabilities in zero-shot and few-shot tasks, and GPTScore harnesses these for evaluation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;Enables More Human-Like Evaluation:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;color: oklch(0.304 0.04 213.681)&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: oklch(0.99 0.004 106.471)&quot;&gt;By using natural language instructions, GPTScore mimics how humans evaluate text, potentially capturing nuanced qualities better than rigid metrics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 32, 32)&quot;&gt;Hallucinated tokens can still receive high probabilities if the preceding context includes similar (but incorrect) information, leading to false confidence. from the paper&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 119, 0)&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 119, 0)&quot;&gt;(A Survey on Hallucination in Large Language Models: Principles, Taxonomy, Challenges, and Open Questions 2025)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 32, 32)&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</rdf:value>
    </bib:Memo>
